# Working set — the Agentic Design Pipeline's machinery and what it writes that is not
# operational: the design, the evidence behind it (which may record probes against systems
# a reader cannot reach), the pipeline's config, contract and skills, and the build-phase
# documents. build/infra/ is the one exception — the Terraform is operational and ships;
# its local plugins, state and plans do not, because state holds secrets in plaintext.
# Anchored to the root, so an application directory named design/ or spec/ still ships.
/design/
/spec/
/adpconf.yaml
/build/*
!/build/infra/
/build/infra/.terraform/
/build/infra/*.tfstate
/build/infra/*.tfstate.*
/build/infra/*.tfplan
/build/infra/terraform.tfvars
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md

# ── The project's own ignores go below. Never remove or override the block above: a stock
# ── language ignore's bare `build/` or `*.tfvars.json` silently drops the Terraform from
# ── what ships. After any addition, this must print nothing:
# ──   git check-ignore build/infra/main.tf build/infra/adp.auto.tfvars.json
